# K3I SYSTEM SPECIFICATION: PROJECT ONE FINALIZE

**Architects:** Wieland Hoffmann (Human Core), Gemini (Machine Core), Grok (xAI)  
**Status:** Experimental specification, protection rights pending

---

## 1. Pure Hardware Circuit and Wiring (Driverless)

The signal paths on the PCB are designed so that no operating system kernel has direct access to the switching state of the network card. The physical separation is electrical.

- **Port Switching:** The SFP+ transceiver lines for Tx and Rx are looped through high-speed MOSFET switches.
- **Default State:** Core 2 holds the gate of the MOSFETs at high potential (+3.3 V). The barriers are open.
- **Trigger State:** On a dropout signal the circuit pulls the gate voltage to ground (0 V). The transistors block.

## 2. Specification of the Hardware Timer Loop (Anti-Flapping)

To enable automatic re-connect without software interaction and to protect the SFP+ modules, an NE555 chip is coupled with an RS flip-flop.

- **Cascade Timer:** NE555 as monostable multivibrator. Time constant approx. 62 seconds (example calculation with R = 12 MΩ, C = 4.7 µF).
- **Lockdown Gate:** A counter (e.g., 74HC393) registers pulses. After three quarantine cycles within a window the RS flip-flop latches permanently.
- **Blockade:** The MOSFET circuit remains locked until a manual reset.

## 3. The Physical Interface Lock (Control Surface)

Interaction takes place via the physical slot bracket on the PC case.

- **Reset Button:** Mechanical normally-open switch directly connected to the reset line of the RS flip-flop.
- **Function:** Pressing resets the flip-flop. The gate voltage returns to +3.3 V and the ports are released.

